<title>BELGIUM: EU CLEARS ADM/ACATOS &amp; HUTCHESON BUY OF SOYA MAINZ.</title>
<headline>EU CLEARS ADM/ACATOS &amp; HUTCHESON BUY OF SOYA MAINZ.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has cleared the acquisition by a German subsidiary of ADM International Ltd and Acatos &amp; Hutcheson Plc of German soya beans processor Soya Mainz GmbH, a Commission source said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The source did not give any details. The Commission is expected to make an official statement in the coming days.</p>
<p>Soya Mainz announced in June it had been sold to Archer-Daniels-Midland's ADM Beteiligungsgesellschaft mbH and Acatos, a British company active in the bottling and canning of vegetable oils.</p>
<p>The German company was previously owned by the Wilh. Werhahn group and Heidelberger Zement AG.</p>
<p>The sale was filed for EU regulatory approval on July 8.</p>
<p>ADM already has a controlling stake in leading German processor Oelmuehle Hamburg AG, which in 1996 crushed 3.10 million tonnes of soybeans. -- Amelia Torres 322 2876841</p>
